ression\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $4\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we first draw the vector $4\\mathbf{b}$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/6a/6af6aff8a4aa111e6eb74f8046a4ec01582c1cee7fcf922e443d17d0348da7f4.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $4\\mathbf{b}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=3|\\mathbf{a}|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-3\\mathbf{a}.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{c} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =4\\mathbf{b}-3\\mathbf{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}=-3\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}∦\\mathbf{b},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186235568 :question/problem "![](images/1d/1d424b5db0534a8d9abc9b0aa84dcb2e6860a7ed51de7390fc4f7e91c1c33f2b.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+4b,$ find $\\lambda .$" "![](images/1d/1d424b5db0534a8d9abc9b0aa84dcb2e6860a7ed51de7390fc4f7e91c1c33f2b.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda \\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b},$ find $\\lambda .$"] [:db/cas 17592186235568 :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+4b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $4b.$ So, we first draw the vector $4b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/d8/d8fdfb800bd9bbb179d51115b86823d99029732fee9810281b9c587a32376993.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $4b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=4|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directi